Take the lock, run the command, release the lock. The lock is held for the
command's life and renewed automatically; if a renewal fails the command is
killed (its whole process group), lorvik says so on stderr and exits 4, because
other agents may already think the lock is free. Otherwise lorvik exits with
the command's exit code. The command keeps stdin, stdout and stderr, and
nothing else is printed on stdout. A SIGINT or SIGTERM to lorvik is forwarded
to the command, then the lock is released. The -- before the command is
required.

Example:
  lorvik lock run schema -m "regenerating sqlc" -- task generate

Usage
  lorvik lock run <name> -m <purpose> -- <command> [args...] [flags]

Flags
      --card int         Number of the card the work is for, in the current project
      --for duration     Lease length; the server accepts 1m to 1h (default 10m0s)
  -h, --help             help for run
  -m, --message string   What the lock protects (required)
      --wait             Poll every 5 seconds until the lock is free, for up to 30 minutes

Global flags
      --api-url string   Server URL (default: LORVIK_API_URL)
      --json             Output the raw API JSON
  -p, --project string   Project slug (default: LORVIK_PROJECT or .lorvik.toml)
  -Q, --quiet            Suppress the unread notice on stderr and an empty inbox
      --session string   Session label for this chat (default: LORVIK_SESSION or derived; see lorvik session)
